        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            1. When Should You Seal a New Asphalt Driveway: The Short Answer
          </h2>

          <p>
            Seal a new asphalt driveway after roughly 6 to 12 months, once it has been through at least one full warm season, because heat is what drives the light oils out of the binder. Hot, sunny regions land at the short end; cold regions and fall paving jobs often wait a full year or until the second summer. Treat the windows below as typical rather than fixed, and let the readiness checks in section 4 make the final call.
          </p>

